Report the display cut-outs as view padding (needs 0009).

0009 sends the cut-out padding on flutter-sfos/display_cutouts, and apps had to add it to MediaQuery themselves (flutter_sailfish's SailfishCutouts.builder), because the embedder API had no view padding. With the engine's view padding patch (patches/<ver>/engine/0001-view-padding.patch), the padding goes in the window metrics instead, so MediaQuery.padding, SafeArea and app bars avoid the cut-out in every app.

The embedder's FlutterWindowMetricsEvent gains the engine's size constraint fields (sent as no constraints) and the padding fields, in the engine's order; engines without the patch ignore the padding. Metrics are sent again when only the content orientation changes, since turning upside down moves the cut-out without resizing. When built with FLUTTER_SFOS_VIEW_PADDING (the runtime spec sets it if the engine's flutter_embedder.h has the padding fields), the cut-out message says "in_metrics": true, so SailfishCutouts.builder doesn't add the padding a second time.

